# CODEOWNERS for the playground repo.
#
# Save this file as either:
#   .github/CODEOWNERS   (preferred; keeps the repo root clean)
#   CODEOWNERS           (also valid)
#   docs/CODEOWNERS      (also valid)
#
# Reviewers must have WRITE access to the repo to be assignable.
# The LAST matching pattern wins (different from .gitignore semantics).
#
# Replace the @-handles below with your actual GitHub username (or a team you
# belong to). For a solo playground repo, replace every entry with @uzair-imtiaz.

# Default owner: catches anything not matched by a more specific rule.
*                                       @uzair-imtiaz

# Application source. In a real repo this would be @arbisoft/app-team.
/sample-app/                            @uzair-imtiaz

# Container build files. In a real repo this would be @arbisoft/platform.
/modules/02-containers/lab/             @uzair-imtiaz

# CI/CD changes. Touchy; route to the platform team and (in real life) security.
/.github/                               @uzair-imtiaz
/.github/workflows/                     @uzair-imtiaz

# Pre-commit config. Affects every contributor's local workflow.
/.pre-commit-config.yaml                @uzair-imtiaz

# CODEOWNERS itself. Changes to who owns what should be reviewed by the same
# people who already own the repo.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @uzair-imtiaz
